-- program.lth: the rules of the checker as the laws of `WellFormed`.
--
-- Draft 0, 2026-10-13, by Claude Opus 5.5 in the session (step 3.1 of
-- record/plan/luthier-from-zero/plan-from-zero-2026-10-13-execution.md). Sources: spec 4, its rules 4.R1 to 4.R13 and the
-- statements 4.S14, 4.S17, 4.S21, 4.S23, 4.S24; spec 1.S7 (D(n), B(n)); spec 5.S9, 5.S10
-- (`Failures E`); L2.7, L14. The pattern is that of ebnf.lth and term.lth.
--
-- What this file states (4.S21). A model of `WellFormed` is a checker: from a program it gives the
-- failures it finds. Each rule of chapter 4 is a predicate, `violates`, written here as the rule
-- says it, and two generic laws, `ReportsViolations` and `ReportsNoFalseFailure`, say the checker reports a failure of that rule
-- for a name exactly when the name violates it. So the rule is stated once, as a predicate, and
-- the checker is held to it; the accept and reject programs of `tests/spec/` are its cases. The
-- Python checker (step 4) is a specimen.
--
-- Which program. The rules read what is written: whether an alias is written with `=` (4.R7),
-- `:=` against `<-` (4.R12), a body that is an `extern` (4.R5). So `WellFormed` takes the surface
-- program of grammar.lth; the rules that need the type of a term (4.R8, 4.R9, 4.R11, 4.R13) read
-- it through a typing, a theory of its own (§4), over the elaborated `Term` of term.lth.
--
-- Index. Status of each section: done, or todo with what it needs. A session or Codex continuing
-- this file takes the first todo, writes it in the pattern of the done ones, checks it with
-- `luthier parse src/luthier/lib/program.lth`, sets its status to done here, and commits.
--
--   §1 Failures and the theory: `Failure`, `Report`, `Elaboration` (translation.lth),
--      `WellFormed` over an alpha, a substitution, an elaboration
--      and a typing, the generic laws `ReportsViolations`, `ReportsNoFalseFailure` (4.S21, 5.S9). done
--   §2 Names: the acts' names, D(n) and B(n) on the surface tree (1.S7). Type and
--      term position (4.S2) still to add, for 4.R2.                                 done
--   §3 The rules that read names and forms: 4.R1, 4.R2 (existence), 4.R3 with L2.7,
--      4.R4, 4.R5, 4.R7, 4.R12 (top level), 4.S14. Still to add: 4.R2 by position and
--      theory, 4.R12 inside blocks.                                                 done
--   §4 Typing: variables, constants, lambda and application, the universe; refinement
--      with variance (4.R9); the branch of a condition (4.R11).                       done
--   §5 The rules that read types: 4.R6, 4.R8, 4.R9. 4.R11 is a law of the typing;
--      4.R13 and 4.S23 are laws of the elaboration (step 2.4).                        done
--   §6 Reports: provisional externs, loose functions (4.S17); 4.R10 and 4.S20 by name
--      only, the author's judgement.                                                  done
--   §7 `WellFormed :=` the conjunction.                                               done

import "grammar.lth" SurfaceProgram SurfaceAct Surface SurfacePattern LambdaParam Item RecordField Binder Body
  Clause ImportName declare define alias importAct operatorAct datum explicit implicit termBody dataBody
  clausesBody name literal universe world app binop neg tuple piSurface sigma sigmaNamed recordSurface
  subtype recordValue block sumSurface list lambda matchOf namedArg ifThen proj quoted pWild pApp pLit pTuple
  plainParam typedParam shapeParam bind rebind
import "term.lth" Term Program Act Constant Pattern Alpha AlphaPair Substitution Var Lit Universe World Lam App Pi
  Sigma Pair Match Inj Sum Data Subtype Extern Primitive Axiom Hole Record RecordValue Proj Let Declare Define Datum IntConst FloatConst
  StringConst PCon PWild

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- §1 Failures and the theory

-- A failure names its rule, the name it is about, and says why (5.S9: a check is written in the
-- form that explains its failures). `Failures E` of 5.S9 is the list of them; its projections are
-- checks.lth's (5.S10, step 3.3).
Failure = { rule : String, name : String, message : String }

-- The elaboration of a surface program into the kernel's `Program` (2.S12, 3.S30) is
-- translation.lth's theory; the rules on types read what a definition elaborates to.
import "translation.lth" Elaboration

-- A checker, held to an elaboration and a typing (§4): the failures it finds in a program
-- (4.S21), and what it reports without rejecting (4.S19, §6).
Report = { kind : String, name : String, message : String }
WellFormed (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (e : Elaboration a) (t : Typing a sb) : {
  check : SurfaceProgram -> List Failure,
  report : SurfaceProgram -> List Report,
}

-- removing a bound name removes the dotted names it prefixes: `c.parse` with `c` a binder is the
-- projection of a bound variable, not a free name (2.S14; check.py, step 4.1)
removeName (x : String) (xs : List String) : List String :=
  filter List String (fn (y : String) { not (x == y or namePrefix y == x) }) xs
removeNames (xs ys : List String) : List String :=
  filter List String (fn (y : String) { not (any List String (fn (x : String) { x == y or namePrefix y == x }) xs) }) ys

reported (fs : List Failure) (rule n : String) : Bool :=
  any List Failure (fn (f : Failure) { f.rule == rule and f.name == n }) fs

-- The programs a rule is tested on, and its two laws (review of layers 0-1, B). A law stated over
-- every program with one of its names would be vacuous in practice: a random program violates
-- some rules almost always and others almost never, so only one side of "exactly" would be seen
-- (L9.6). So each rule has two domains, the programs with a name that violates it and those with
-- a name that does not, and two laws. Their generators are the certifier's (7.R1): the accept and
-- reject programs of tests/spec/ as a census, and well-formed programs drawn from a small pool of
-- names and changed by one edit aimed at the rule. A predicate that states only part of its rule
-- (4.R2, 4.R12 at the top level, the rules on types until `Typing` is complete) under-approximates
-- the violations, so only its sound direction, "violates implies reported", is a law: "exactly"
-- would fail a checker that implements the whole rule.
Violating (violates : SurfaceProgram -> String -> Bool) : U :=
  { p : SurfaceProgram, n : String | member List String n (actNames p) and violates p n }
Clean (violates : SurfaceProgram -> String -> Bool) : U :=
  { p : SurfaceProgram, n : String | member List String n (actNames p) and not (violates p n) }
ReportsViolations (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (e : Elaboration a) (t : Typing a sb) (rule : String)
                  (violates : SurfaceProgram -> String -> Bool) (w : WellFormed a sb e t) (c : Violating violates) : Bool :=
  reported (w.check c.p) rule c.n
ReportsNoFalseFailure (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (e : Elaboration a) (t : Typing a sb) (rule : String)
                      (violates : SurfaceProgram -> String -> Bool) (w : WellFormed a sb e t) (c : Clean violates) : Bool :=
  not (reported (w.check c.p) rule c.n)
-- and it reports nothing about names the program does not introduce
ReportsOnItsNames (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (e : Elaboration a) (t : Typing a sb) (w : WellFormed a sb e t)
                  (p : SurfaceProgram) : Bool := failuresNamed (w.check p) (actNames p)
failuresNamed (fs : List Failure) (ns : List String) : Bool :=
  all List Failure (fn (f : Failure) { member List String f.name ns }) fs

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- §2 Names

-- the name an act introduces, if any, and the names of a program
actName (a : SurfaceAct) : Maybe String := match a {
  declare x bs t -> just x ; define x bs t b -> just x ; alias x bs t -> just x ;
  importAct f ns -> nothing ; operatorAct o t -> nothing ; datum t -> nothing ;
}
actNames (p : SurfaceProgram) : List String :=
  concat String (map (fn (a : SurfaceAct) { match actName a { nothing -> nil ; just x -> [x] } }) p)
importedNames (p : SurfaceProgram) : List String :=
  concat String (map (fn (a : SurfaceAct) { match a { importAct f ns -> importNames ns ; _ -> nil } }) p)
importNames (ns : List ImportName) : List String :=
  map (fn (i : ImportName) { match i.asName { nothing -> i.name ; just y -> y } }) ns

isDeclared (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  any List SurfaceAct (fn (a : SurfaceAct) { match a { declare x bs t -> x == n ; _ -> false } }) p
isDefined (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  any List SurfaceAct (fn (a : SurfaceAct) { match a { define x bs t b -> x == n ; _ -> false } }) p
isAlias (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  any List SurfaceAct (fn (a : SurfaceAct) { match a { alias x bs t -> x == n ; _ -> false } }) p
-- a name is known when the program introduces it, imports it, makes it a constructor, or core
-- gives it (`core` the list of core's names: core is not written yet, 12.S21). A dotted name
-- `m.f` is known when the whole name is, or its first part (2.S14: a qualified name, or a
-- projection of a variable or definition); `namePrefix` gives the part before the first `.`, and
-- the name itself when it has none (a function of core's `String`, 11, declared here until core
-- names it; review of layers 0-1, B).
namePrefix : String -> String
knownName (core : List String) (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  knownWhole core p n or knownWhole core p (namePrefix n)
knownWhole (core : List String) (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  member List String n (actNames p) or member List String n (importedNames p) or member List String n (constructors p) or member List String n core

-- The constructors of the `data` of a program: a pattern `name` is one of them if it names one,
-- and a variable otherwise (2.S10, 2.S13).
-- (a label of a labeled sum, `{ a : A || b : B }`, named by an alias or a definition, is its
-- injection, and so a constructor here; check.py, step 4.1)
constructors (p : SurfaceProgram) : List String :=
  concat String (map (fn (a : SurfaceAct) { match a {
    define x bs t b -> ((bodyConstructors b) <> (typeLabels t)) ;
    alias x bs t -> sumLabels t ;
    declare x bs t -> ((sumLabels t) <> (binderLabels bs)) ;
    _ -> nil } }) p)
-- the labels of a labeled sum anywhere in a term are its injections, used as constructors where
-- the sum is written in a type: `{ one : A || two : B }` in a field's type (check.py, bite 2)
sumLabels (t : Surface) : List String := ((match t { sumSurface kvs -> surfacePairNames kvs ; _ -> nil }) <> (sumLabelsIn (children t)))
sumLabelsIn (ts : List Surface) : List String := concat String (map sumLabels ts)
typeLabels (t : Maybe Surface) : List String := match t { nothing -> nil ; just u -> sumLabels u }
binderLabels (bs : List Binder) : List String :=
  concat String (map (fn (b : Binder) { match b { explicit xs t d -> sumLabels t ; implicit xs t -> sumLabels t } }) bs)
bodyConstructors (b : Body) : List String := match b { dataBody cs -> surfacePairNames cs ; termBody t -> sumLabels t ; clausesBody cs -> nil }
surfacePairNames (kvs : List (String * Surface)) : List String := map (fn (kv : String * Surface) { match kv { (k, v) -> k } }) kvs

-- the variables a pattern binds, given the constructors `k`
patternBinds (k : List String) (q : SurfacePattern) : List String := match q {
  pWild -> nil ; pLit l -> nil ;
  pApp n qs -> if member List String n k then patternsBind k qs else (match qs { nil -> [n] ; _ -> patternsBind k qs }) ;
  pTuple qs -> patternsBind k qs ;
}
patternsBind (k : List String) (qs : List SurfacePattern) : List String := concat String (map (patternBinds k) qs)

-- spec 1.S7: the names found in a term, less those it binds; operators are core's and not counted
namesIn (k : List String) (t : Surface) : List String := match t {
  name s -> [s] ;
  literal l -> nil ; universe -> nil ; world -> nil ;
  app f a -> ((namesIn k f) <> (namesIn k a)) ;
  binop o a b -> ((namesIn k a) <> (namesIn k b)) ;
  neg a -> namesIn k a ; quoted a -> namesIn k a ; namedArg x a -> namesIn k a ; proj a x -> namesIn k a ;
  tuple ts -> namesInAll k ts ; list ts -> namesInAll k ts ;
  piSurface xs a b -> ((namesIn k a) <> (removeNames xs (namesIn k b))) ;
  sigma xs a b -> ((namesIn k a) <> (removeNames xs (namesIn k b))) ;
  sigmaNamed x a y b -> ((namesIn k a) <> (removeName x (namesIn k b))) ;
  recordSurface fs law -> ((fieldsNames k fs) <> (match law { nothing -> nil ; just l -> removeNames (fieldLabels fs) (namesIn k l) })) ;
  subtype q a law -> ((namesIn k a) <> (removeNames (patternBinds k q) (namesIn k law))) ;
  recordValue kvs -> pairsNames k kvs ; sumSurface kvs -> pairsNames k kvs ;
  block items e -> itemsNames k items e ;
  lambda ps items e -> ((paramsNames k ps) <> (removeNames (paramsBind k ps) (itemsNames k items e))) ;
  matchOf s arms -> ((namesIn k s) <> (armsNames k arms)) ;
  ifThen c a b -> ((namesIn k c) <> (((namesIn k a) <> (match b { nothing -> nil ; just e -> namesIn k e })))) ;
}
namesInAll (k : List String) (ts : List Surface) : List String := concat String (map (namesIn k) ts)
pairsNames (k : List String) (kvs : List (String * Surface)) : List String :=
  concat String (map (fn (kv : String * Surface) { match kv { (x, v) -> namesIn k v } }) kvs)
fieldLabels (fs : List RecordField) : List String := concat String (map (fn (f : RecordField) { f.names }) fs)
-- a field's names are in scope in the fields after it (a dependent record, 2.S14)
-- kept as a recursion (bite 13b): a telescope: each entry's names bind in what follows it, so the tail is rewritten by the head; no fold of a monoid says that
fieldsNames (k : List String) (fs : List RecordField) : List String :=
  match fs { nil -> nil ; cons f rest -> ((namesIn k f.type) <> (removeNames f.names (fieldsNames k rest))) }
-- a block's items bind in what follows them
-- kept as a recursion (bite 13b): a telescope: each entry's names bind in what follows it, so the tail is rewritten by the head; no fold of a monoid says that
itemsNames (k : List String) (items : List Item) (e : Surface) : List String := match items {
  nil -> namesIn k e ;
  cons it rest -> match it {
    bind x t -> ((namesIn k t) <> (removeName x (itemsNames k rest e))) ;
    rebind q t -> ((namesIn k t) <> (removeNames (patternBinds k q) (itemsNames k rest e))) } }
paramsBind (k : List String) (ps : List LambdaParam) : List String :=
  concat String (map (fn (q : LambdaParam) { match q { plainParam x -> [x] ; typedParam xs t -> xs ; shapeParam qs -> patternsBind k qs } }) ps)
-- a parameter's names are in scope in the parameters after it
-- kept as a recursion (bite 13b): a telescope: each entry's names bind in what follows it, so the tail is rewritten by the head; no fold of a monoid says that
paramsNames (k : List String) (ps : List LambdaParam) : List String := match ps { nil -> nil ;
  cons q rest -> ((match q { typedParam xs t -> namesIn k t ; _ -> nil }) <> (removeNames (paramsBind k [q]) (paramsNames k rest))) }
armsNames (k : List String) (arms : List (SurfacePattern * Surface)) : List String :=
  concat String (map (fn (arm : SurfacePattern * Surface) { match arm { (q, b) -> removeNames (patternBinds k q) (namesIn k b) } }) arms)

-- D(n) and B(n) of 1.S7: the names in the declared type of `n` (its binders included) and in its
-- body, each less the binders' own names
-- a binder's names are in scope in the binders after it: `(a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a)`, a
-- default mentioning an earlier parameter, `{A : U} (x : A)` (2.S7, 2.S16)
-- kept as a recursion (bite 13b): a telescope: each entry's names bind in what follows it, so the tail is rewritten by the head; no fold of a monoid says that
binderNames (k : List String) (bs : List Binder) : List String := match bs { nil -> nil ;
  cons b rest -> ((match b { explicit xs t d -> ((namesIn k t) <> (match d { nothing -> nil ; just e -> namesIn k e })) ;
                                   implicit xs t -> namesIn k t }) <> (removeNames (binderBound [b]) (binderNames k rest))) }
binderBound (bs : List Binder) : List String :=
  concat String (map (fn (b : Binder) { match b { explicit xs t d -> xs ; implicit xs t -> xs } }) bs)
bodyNames (k : List String) (b : Body) : List String := match b {
  termBody t -> namesIn k t ;
  dataBody cs -> pairsNames k cs ;
  clausesBody cs -> clausesNames k cs ;
}
clausesNames (k : List String) (cs : List Clause) : List String :=
  concat String (map (fn (c : Clause) { removeNames (patternsBind k c.patterns) (namesIn k c.body) }) cs)
dOf (p : SurfaceProgram) (a : SurfaceAct) : List String := match a {
  declare x bs t -> ((binderNames (constructors p) bs) <> (removeNames (binderBound bs) (namesIn (constructors p) t))) ;
  define x bs t b -> ((binderNames (constructors p) bs) <> (match t { nothing -> nil ; just u -> removeNames (binderBound bs) (namesIn (constructors p) u) })) ;
  alias x bs t -> ((binderNames (constructors p) bs) <> (removeNames (binderBound bs) (namesIn (constructors p) t))) ;
  _ -> nil ;
}
bOf (p : SurfaceProgram) (a : SurfaceAct) : List String := match a {
  define x bs t b -> removeNames (binderBound bs) (bodyNames (constructors p) b) ;
  _ -> nil ;
}

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- §3 The rules that read names and forms

-- core's names: core encloses every file (12.S21) and is not written yet, so its names are a hole
coreNames : List String

actsNamed (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : List SurfaceAct :=
  filter List SurfaceAct (fn (a : SurfaceAct) { match actName a { just x -> x == n ; nothing -> false } }) p
countName (n : String) (xs : List String) : Nat := count List String (fn (x : String) { x == n }) xs
definedNames (p : SurfaceProgram) : List String :=
  concat String (map (fn (a : SurfaceAct) { match a { define x bs t b -> [x] ; _ -> nil } }) p)

-- 4.R1: a declaration mentions only names that exist, declared or defined (or imported, or core's)
violatesR1 (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  any List SurfaceAct (fn a { match a { declare x bs t -> any List String (fn (m : String) { not (knownName coreNames p m) }) (dOf p a) ; _ -> false } }) (actsNamed p n)

-- 4.R2, the part that reads names: the names a definition mentions exist. That a name in type
-- position is defined unless it is in the definition's own theory needs type position (4.S2) and
-- the theories (4.S3, the strongly connected components): todo, §2.
violatesR2Exists (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  any List SurfaceAct (fn a { match a { define x bs t b -> any List String (fn (m : String) { not (knownName coreNames p m) }) (((dOf p a) <> (bOf p a))) ; _ -> false } }) (actsNamed p n)

-- 4.R3: a predicate touches what it is over: every label of a record with a law, the variables of
-- a subtype's pattern (a pattern that binds nothing constrains nothing: `{ _ : T | true }`), the
-- parameter of a lambda predicate; every field of a theory declared by its record and defined by
-- a conjunction of laws; and (L2.7, D-2026-10-13-p) every constructor of a `data`, mentioned by
-- some law. A law is a definition a theory claims: one named in the `&`-conjunction that defines
-- a theory (4.S14), not any definition at `Bool`, which would count helpers and miss laws at
-- `Failures E` or with parameters (review of layers 0-1, B). Whether the law states the
-- constructor's role, and not only lists it, a test cannot decide (4.S19 reports it). A rule
-- violated by any constructor without such a law rejects (D-2026-10-13-aa, Q3).
-- 4.R3 with 1.S7: "a projection `e.f` counts what e contains", so a dotted name `v.n` touches `v`
-- (`namesIn` gives `v.n` whole). [proposed] Reading 1.S7's occurrence as 4.R3's touch: arrays.lth's
-- `VecOf`, `{ v : Vec A | v.n == k }`, touches `v` (report of the leftovers agent, f8c5f40).
untouched (k : List String) (labels : List String) (law : Surface) : Bool :=
  any List String (fn (l : String) { not (touchesName l (namesIn k law)) }) labels
touchesName (l : String) (ns : List String) : Bool :=
  any List String (fn (m : String) { m == l or namePrefix m == l }) ns
predicateUntouched (k : List String) (isPredicate : Bool) (t : Surface) : Bool := match t {
  recordSurface fs law -> match law { nothing -> false ; just l -> untouched k (fieldLabels fs) l } ;
  subtype q a law -> (match patternBinds k q { nil -> true ; vs -> untouched k vs law }) ;
  lambda ps items e -> isPredicate and untouched k (paramsBind k ps) (block items e) ;
  _ -> false ;
}
-- 4.R3 is a rule on predicates, so a lambda is held to touch its parameters when it is one: when
-- the type written on its definition ends in `Bool`, `Law` or `Failures E` (5.S9); with no type
-- written, when the name is declared at a type that is not a function, whose body a lambda can
-- only be as its predicate (4.R6: `Tagged := fn p { true }`), or at one that ends so; and when
-- nothing is written (a type to infer). A function to anything else may leave a parameter unread:
-- generators.lth's `walk`, a `Gen` that does not read the size, and the grammar has no `_`
-- parameter for `fn` (group 5 of record/IA/check-2026-10-13/opus-3b.md, part 2). A predicate type
-- reached through an alias (`P = A -> Bool`) is not seen on the surface; the checker, which
-- expands aliases first (4.R7), sees it.
endsInVerdict (t : Surface) : Bool := match t {
  binop o a b -> o == "->" and endsInVerdict b ;
  piSurface xs a b -> endsInVerdict b ;
  name s -> s == "Bool" or s == "Law" ;
  app f a -> headName t == just "Failures" or headName t == just "Law" ;
  _ -> false ;
}
isArrow (t : Surface) : Bool := match t { binop o a b -> o == "->" ; piSurface xs a b -> true ; _ -> false }
lambdaIsPredicate (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) (t : Maybe Surface) : Bool := match t {
  just u -> endsInVerdict u ;
  nothing -> (match declaredSurface p n { nothing -> true ; just d -> not (isArrow d) or endsInVerdict d }) }
-- the names a conjunction of laws claims: each conjunct's head name
conjuncts (t : Surface) : List String := match t {
  binop o l r -> if o == "&" then ((conjuncts l) <> (conjuncts r)) else nil ;
  app f x -> conjuncts f ;
  name s -> [s] ;
  _ -> nil ;
}
isConjunction (t : Surface) : Bool := match t { binop o l r -> o == "&" ; _ -> false }
-- the definitions that define a theory by laws: a conjunction, or the definition of a name
-- declared as a theory (`T : { ... }` then `T := L`)
-- (a declaration anywhere in the program makes a definition of that name a head; check.py found the
-- search ran on what followed the definition only)
theoryHeads (whole acts : SurfaceProgram) : List SurfaceAct :=
  filter List SurfaceAct (fn (act : SurfaceAct) { match act {
    define x bs t b -> (match b { termBody u -> isConjunction u or isDeclared whole x ; _ -> false }) ;
    _ -> false } }) acts
claimedLaws (p : SurfaceProgram) : List String := claimedBy (theoryHeads p p)
claimedBy (hs : List SurfaceAct) : List String :=
  concat String (map (fn (h : SurfaceAct) { match h { define x bs t b -> (match b { termBody u -> conjuncts u ; _ -> nil }) ; _ -> nil } }) hs)
-- the names the claimed laws' bodies mention, and the constructors their own matches name.
-- [proposed] A match in a law's body states what holds for each constructor it names (test.lth's
-- `CountsCases`: a sampled run has exactly the cases asked), and for a constructor whose payload
-- has no `==` it is the only way a law can name it (4.R8: `SampledMode` holds a `Placement`, a record
-- of functions). A helper the law calls is still not read (4.S15: a law depends on the names in
-- it, without unfolding definitions), and an observer that only lists the constructors is such a
-- helper (4.R3). Group 2 of record/IA/check-2026-10-13/opus-3b.md, part 2.
lawNames (p : SurfaceProgram) : List String := lawBodies p (claimedLaws p) p
lawBodies (p : SurfaceProgram) (laws : List String) (acts : SurfaceProgram) : List String :=
  concat String (map (fn (act : SurfaceAct) { match act {
    define x bs t b -> if member List String x laws then ((bOf p act) <> (bodyMatched (constructors p) b)) else nil ;
    _ -> nil } }) acts)
-- the constructors named by the patterns of the matches and clauses of a body, given the constructors `k`
bodyMatched (k : List String) (b : Body) : List String := match b {
  termBody u -> matchedIn k u ; clausesBody cs -> clausesMatched k cs ; dataBody cs -> nil }
clausesMatched (k : List String) (cs : List Clause) : List String :=
  concat String (map (fn (c : Clause) { ((patternsNamed k c.patterns) <> (matchedIn k c.body)) }) cs)
matchedIn (k : List String) (t : Surface) : List String :=
  ((match t { matchOf s arms -> armsMatched k arms ; _ -> nil }) <> (matchedInAll k (children t)))
matchedInAll (k : List String) (ts : List Surface) : List String := concat String (map (matchedIn k) ts)
armsMatched (k : List String) (arms : List (SurfacePattern * Surface)) : List String :=
  concat String (map (fn (arm : SurfacePattern * Surface) { match arm { (q, b) -> patternNamed k q } }) arms)
patternNamed (k : List String) (q : SurfacePattern) : List String := match q {
  pWild -> nil ; pLit l -> nil ;
  pApp n qs -> if member List String n k then cons n (patternsNamed k qs) else patternsNamed k qs ;
  pTuple qs -> patternsNamed k qs ;
}
patternsNamed (k : List String) (qs : List SurfacePattern) : List String := concat String (map (patternNamed k) qs)
-- a field of a declared theory is touched when a claimed law reads it as `m.field`. A law reads
-- its model through the model's binder, so a dotted name there is rooted at that binder and the
-- field of the model is the part after the first `.`: `s.world.read` reads the field `world` of
-- `s`, and `read` is a field of that field's own theory (group 1 of
-- record/IA/check-2026-10-13/opus-3b.md, part 2: the part after the last `.` counted `read` only).
-- `nameRest` gives the part after the first `.` (a function of core's `String`, declared until
-- core names it), and `namePrefix` of it is the field.
nameRest : String -> String
fieldsOfDeclared (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : List String :=
  match lookup List String (List String) n (concat (String * List String) (map (fn (act : SurfaceAct) {
    match act { declare x bs t -> [(x, (match t { recordSurface fs law -> fieldLabels fs ; _ -> nil }))] ; _ -> nil } }) p)) {
    nothing -> nil ; just fs -> fs }
-- the fields a term reads: the field after the first `.` of every dotted name, and every projection,
-- bound or not, since a law reads a field through its model parameter, `m.parse` (check.py, bite 2:
-- `lawNames` removes what a binder binds, so the reads through `m` were lost)
fieldsRead (t : Surface) : List String := ((match t {
    name s -> if namePrefix s == s then nil else [namePrefix (nameRest s)] ;
    proj a x -> [x] ;
    _ -> nil }) <> (fieldsReadIn (children t)))
fieldsReadIn (ts : List Surface) : List String := concat String (map fieldsRead ts)
lawReads (p : SurfaceProgram) : List String := lawReadsIn (claimedLaws p) p
lawReadsIn (laws : List String) (acts : SurfaceProgram) : List String :=
  concat String (map (fn (act : SurfaceAct) { match act {
    define x bs t b -> if member List String x laws then ((bindersReads bs) <> (bodyReads b)) else nil ;
    _ -> nil } }) acts)
-- 4.R3 with 1.S7: "the annotation of a binder" is an occurrence (in type position), so a law reads
-- the fields its binders' types and defaults name, as it reads those of its body. [proposed]
-- Reading 1.S7 for 4.R3's reads: tables.lth's `NoCellsOffSchema (t : Table) (c : String) (r : Fin
-- t.nRows)` reads `nRows` (report of the leftovers agent, f8c5f40).
bindersReads (bs : List Binder) : List String :=
  concat String (map (fn (b : Binder) { match b { explicit xs t d -> ((fieldsRead t) <> (match d { nothing -> nil ; just e -> fieldsRead e })) ;
                                   implicit xs t -> fieldsRead t } }) bs)
bodyReads (b : Body) : List String := match b {
  termBody u -> fieldsRead u ; clausesBody cs -> clausesReads cs ; dataBody cs -> nil }
clausesReads (cs : List Clause) : List String := concat String (map (fn (c : Clause) { fieldsRead c.body }) cs)
untouchedFields (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  isDeclared p n and isDefined p n and any List String (fn (x : String) { not (member List String x (lawReads p)) }) (fieldsOfDeclared p n)
violatesR3 (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  untouchedFields p n
  or any List SurfaceAct (fn a { match a {
    define x bs t b -> (match b { termBody u -> predicateUntouched (constructors p) (lambdaIsPredicate p x t) u ;
                                  dataBody cs -> any List String (fn (c : String) { not (member List String c (lawNames p)) }) (surfacePairNames cs) ; _ -> false }) ;
    _ -> false } }) (actsNamed p n)

-- the declared type of a name: the one its definition writes, or its declaration's when the
-- definition writes none (`P : U` then `P := ...`; review of layers 0-1, B)
typeOfAct (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) (t : Maybe Surface) : Maybe Surface :=
  match t { just u -> just u ; nothing -> declaredSurface p n }
declaredSurface (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Maybe Surface :=
  lookup List String Surface n (concat (String * Surface) (map (fn (act : SurfaceAct) { match act { declare x bs t -> [(x, t)] ; _ -> nil } }) p))
atUniverse (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) (t : Maybe Surface) : Bool := typeOfAct p n t == just universe

-- 4.R4: a definition at `U` makes a new type only if its body is a subtype with a predicate, a
-- record with a law, or a `data` (a whitelist, as the rule reads); any other body at `U`, an
-- anonymous structure or a type already named, is to be an alias. An extern is 4.R5's. A
-- `primitive` makes a type as 11.R1 prescribes: "`Int : U := primitive "integer"`, `Real : U :=
-- primitive "real"`, ... `String : U := primitive "unicode"`"; that it is allowed only in
-- `core.lut` (11.R2) is a rule on files, not read here.
makesAType (b : Body) : Bool := match b {
  dataBody cs -> true ;
  termBody u -> (match u { subtype q a law -> true ; recordSurface fs law -> not (law == nothing) ; _ -> isExtern u or isPrimitive u }) ;
  clausesBody cs -> false ;
}
violatesR4 (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  any List SurfaceAct (fn act { match act { define x bs t b -> atUniverse p n t and not (makesAType b) ; _ -> false } }) (actsNamed p n)

-- 4.R5: an extern gives a value, never a type, unless it is provisional
isExtern (t : Surface) : Bool := match t { app f a -> isExtern f ; name s -> s == "extern" ; _ -> false }
-- 11.R1: a body `primitive "..."` states what the interpreter provides
isPrimitive (t : Surface) : Bool := match t { app f a -> isPrimitive f ; name s -> s == "primitive" ; _ -> false }
isProvisionalExtern (t : Surface) : Bool :=
  match t { app f a -> (match a { namedArg x v -> x == "provisional" ; _ -> false }) or isProvisionalExtern f ; _ -> false }
-- and its type must be defined (4.R2 applies to an extern as to any body)
violatesR5 (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  any List SurfaceAct (fn act { match act { define x bs t b ->
    (match b { termBody u -> isExtern u and not (isProvisionalExtern u) ; _ -> false })
    and (atUniverse p n t or (match typeOfAct p n t { just ty -> any List String (fn (m : String) { not (isDefined p m or isAlias p m or member List String m coreNames or member List String m (constructors p)) }) (namesIn (constructors p) ty) ;
                                                        nothing -> false })) ;
    _ -> false } }) (actsNamed p n)

-- a name of a type that is neither defined nor core's: what an extern's type may not mention, in
-- an arrow or anywhere in it (check.py, step 4.1)

-- the parts of a surface term, for the rules that look for a form anywhere in a body
children (t : Surface) : List Surface := match t {
  app f x -> [f, x] ; binop o l r -> [l, r] ; neg x -> [x] ; quoted x -> [x] ; namedArg y x -> [x] ; proj x y -> [x] ;
  tuple ts -> ts ; list ts -> ts ; recordValue kvs -> pairValues kvs ; sumSurface kvs -> pairValues kvs ;
  piSurface xs a b -> [a, b] ; sigma xs a b -> [a, b] ; sigmaNamed x a y b -> [a, b] ; subtype q a l -> [a, l] ;
  recordSurface fs l -> ((fieldTypes fs) <> (match l { nothing -> nil ; just u -> [u] })) ;
  block items e -> cons e (itemValues items) ; lambda ps items e -> cons e (itemValues items) ;
  matchOf x arms -> cons x (armBodies arms) ;
  ifThen c x m -> cons c (cons x (match m { nothing -> nil ; just y -> [y] })) ;
  _ -> nil }
fieldTypes (fs : List RecordField) : List Surface := map (fn (f : RecordField) { f.type }) fs
itemValues (items : List Item) : List Surface := map (fn (it : Item) { match it { bind x v -> v ; rebind q v -> v } }) items
armBodies (arms : List (SurfacePattern * Surface)) : List Surface := map (fn (arm : SurfacePattern * Surface) { match arm { (q, b) -> b } }) arms
-- kept as a recursion (bite 13b): a search over the subterms of one term (its children), not over a list; the name is the family's
anyTerm (f : Surface -> Bool) (t : Surface) : Bool := f t or any List Surface (anyTerm f) (children t)
inBody (f : Surface -> Bool) (b : Body) : Bool := match b { termBody u -> anyTerm f u ; clausesBody cs -> any List Clause (fn (c : Clause) { anyTerm f c.body }) cs ; _ -> false }

-- 2.R1: an argument by name names a parameter of the function it is passed to: the head of the
-- application is a name of the program, and its binders hold that name (check.py, step 4.1)
headName (t : Surface) : Maybe String := match t { app f x -> headName f ; name s -> just s ; _ -> nothing }
namedArgsOf (t : Surface) : List String := match t {
  app f x -> ((namedArgsOf f) <> (match x { namedArg y v -> [y] ; _ -> nil })) ; _ -> nil }
parametersOf (p : SurfaceProgram) (f : String) : List String :=
  match lookup List String (List String) f (concat (String * List String) (map (fn (act : SurfaceAct) { match act {
    declare x bs t -> [(x, binderBound bs)] ;
    define x bs t b -> if nonEmptyBinders bs then [(x, binderBound bs)] else nil ;
    _ -> nil } }) p)) { nothing -> nil ; just ns -> ns }
unknownNamedArg (p : SurfaceProgram) (t : Surface) : Bool := match headName t {
  nothing -> false ;
  just f -> member List String f (actNames p) and any List String (fn (x : String) { not (member List String x (parametersOf p f)) }) (namedArgsOf t) }
violatesR2R1 (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  any List SurfaceAct (fn act { match act { define x bs t b -> inBody (unknownNamedArg p) b ; _ -> false } }) (actsNamed p n)

-- 2.R6: in a file, a `<-` whose previous binding of the same name was never used is an error
-- ("unused binding"); a session allows and reports it (check.py, step 4.1). `pending` holds the
-- names bound and not yet used, the definition's parameters first.
removeUsed (pending : List String) (v : Surface) : List String :=
  filter List String (fn (y : String) { not (member List String y (namesIn nil v)) }) pending
-- kept as a recursion (bite 13b): scans items carrying the pending names forward, each item changing what the next sees (state threaded left to right)
unusedRebinding (pending : List String) (items : List Item) : Bool := match items { nil -> false ;
  cons it rest -> match it {
    bind x v -> unusedRebinding (removeUsed pending v) rest ;
    rebind q v -> any List String (fn (x : String) { member List String x (removeUsed pending v) }) (patternBinds nil q)
                  or unusedRebinding (((patternBinds nil q) <> (removeUsed pending v))) rest } }
blockUnused (params : List String) (t : Surface) : Bool := match t {
  block items e -> unusedRebinding params items ;
  lambda ps items e -> unusedRebinding (paramsBind nil ps) items ;
  _ -> false }
violatesR2R6 (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  any List SurfaceAct (fn act { match act { define x bs t b -> inBody (blockUnused (binderBound bs)) b ; _ -> false } }) (actsNamed p n)

-- 4.R13: one meaning of an operator per argument types: two `operator` acts that bind one symbol
-- to two functions of the same declared type are two models of one type (D-2026-10-11-j); reported
-- under the name of each function (check.py, step 4.1). 4.R13: "a second meaning of an operator on
-- the same types refused". The declared type is `typeOfAct`'s, the one the definition writes or else
-- its declaration's: `declaredSurface` alone is `nothing` whenever the type is written on the
-- definition, so any two such functions looked alike (core.lut's `intPlus` and `floatPlus`; report
-- of the leftovers agent, f8c5f40). [proposed] The types of a definition's binders are part of its
-- declared type, compared in order; two spellings of one type (`(a : Int) : Int` and `: Int ->
-- Int`) still differ on the surface, which the checker, comparing elaborated types, does not.
signatureOf (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : List Surface * Maybe Surface := signatureIn p p n
signatureIn (whole acts : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : List Surface * Maybe Surface :=
  match lookup List String (List Surface * Maybe Surface) n (concat (String * (List Surface * Maybe Surface)) (map (fn (act : SurfaceAct) {
    match act { define x bs t b -> [(x, (binderTypes bs, typeOfAct whole x t))] ; _ -> nil } }) acts)) {
    nothing -> (nil, declaredSurface whole n) ; just s -> s }
binderTypes (bs : List Binder) : List Surface :=
  concat Surface (map (fn (b : Binder) { match b { explicit xs t d -> repeatFor xs t ; implicit xs t -> repeatFor xs t } }) bs)
repeatFor (xs : List String) (t : Surface) : List Surface := map (fn (x : String) { t }) xs
operatorBindings (p : SurfaceProgram) : List (String * String) :=
  concat (String * String) (map (fn (act : SurfaceAct) { match act {
    operatorAct o t -> (match t { name f -> [(o, f)] ; _ -> nil }) ;
    _ -> nil } }) p)
rivalModel (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) (bs : List (String * String)) (o : String) : Bool :=
  any List (String * String) (fn (b : String * String) { match b { (o2, g) -> o2 == o and not (g == n) and signatureOf p g == signatureOf p n } }) bs
violatesR13 (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool := bindsTwice p n (operatorBindings p) (operatorBindings p)
bindsTwice (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) (all bs : List (String * String)) : Bool :=
  any List (String * String) (fn (b : String * String) { match b { (o, f) -> f == n and rivalModel p n all o } }) bs

-- 4.R7: an alias is neither declared nor defined
violatesR7 (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool := isAlias p n and (isDeclared p n or isDefined p n)

-- 4.R12: `:=` defines once, at the top level and in blocks: a `:=` of a name already defined in
-- an enclosing scope is an error, and so is a `<-` of a name first bound with `:=`; a parameter of
-- the enclosing definition, or of a lambda, may be rebound (2.S17; review of layers 0-1, B)
violatesR12 (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  countName n (definedNames p) >= 2
  or any List SurfaceAct (fn act { match act {
       define x bs t b -> (match b { termBody u -> blockFault (actNames p) (binderBound bs) u ; _ -> false }) ;
       _ -> false } }) (actsNamed p n)
-- `defined`: the names bound with `:=` in scope; `params`: parameters, which `<-` may rebind
blockFault (defined params : List String) (t : Surface) : Bool := match t {
  block items e -> itemsFault defined params items e ;
  lambda ps items e -> itemsFault defined (((paramsBind nil ps) <> params)) items e ;
  app f x -> blockFault defined params f or blockFault defined params x ;
  binop o l r -> blockFault defined params l or blockFault defined params r ;
  neg x -> blockFault defined params x ; quoted x -> blockFault defined params x ;
  namedArg y x -> blockFault defined params x ; proj x y -> blockFault defined params x ;
  ifThen c x m -> blockFault defined params c or blockFault defined params x
                  or (match m { nothing -> false ; just y -> blockFault defined params y }) ;
  matchOf s arms -> blockFault defined params s or armsFault defined params arms ;
  tuple ts -> any List Surface (blockFault defined params) ts ; list ts -> any List Surface (blockFault defined params) ts ;
  recordValue kvs -> any List Surface (blockFault defined params) (pairValues kvs) ;
  _ -> false ;
}
-- kept as a recursion (bite 13b): scans items carrying the names bound so far forward (state threaded left to right)
itemsFault (defined params : List String) (items : List Item) (e : Surface) : Bool := match items {
  nil -> blockFault defined params e ;
  cons it rest -> match it {
    bind x v -> member List String x defined or blockFault defined params v or itemsFault (cons x defined) params rest e ;
    rebind q v -> any List String (fn (x : String) { member List String x defined }) (patternBinds nil q) or blockFault defined params v
                  or itemsFault defined (((patternBinds nil q) <> params)) rest e } }
armsFault (defined params : List String) (arms : List (SurfacePattern * Surface)) : Bool :=
  any List (SurfacePattern * Surface) (fn (arm : SurfacePattern * Surface) { match arm { (q, b) -> blockFault defined params b } }) arms
pairValues (kvs : List (String * Surface)) : List Surface := map (fn (kv : String * Surface) { match kv { (k, v) -> v } }) kvs

-- 4.S14: a law no type claims defines nothing; it is a branch, and 4.R2 applies to it, so it is
-- reported, not rejected (§6; review of layers 0-1, B). Read, as in 4.R3, as a definition at
-- `Bool` that no other definition's body mentions.
otherBodies (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : List String :=
  concat String (map (fn (a : SurfaceAct) { match a { define x bs t b -> if x == n then nil else bOf p a ; _ -> nil } }) p)
violatesS14 (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  any List SurfaceAct (fn a { match a { define x bs t b -> t == just (name "Bool") and not (member List String n (otherBodies p n)) ; _ -> false } })
         (actsNamed p n)

-- 4.S17, no loose functions, rejects only once local definitions exist; until then it is a report
-- (§6), and the theory files themselves hold such helpers, as 12.S23 allows.


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- §4 Typing

-- The type of an elaborated term in a program and a context of typed variables, if it has one;
-- `same`, the definitional equality of types (3.S20); `refines`, that a value of the first type
-- passes where the second is expected (3.S6, 4.R9); `branchContext`, the context inside the
-- `true` or `false` branch of a condition (4.R11). Only what the rules of §5 need is stated; the
-- type formers of 3 §2 get their roles here, as the computing constructors got theirs from
-- `Reduction` (term.lth).
Context = List (String * Term)
Typing (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) : {
  typeOf : Program -> Context -> Term -> Maybe Term,
  same : Term -> Term -> Bool,
  refines : Term -> Term -> Bool,
  branchContext : Context -> Term -> Bool -> Context,
}

typed (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (r : Maybe Term) (ty : Term) : Bool :=
  match r { nothing -> false ; just u -> t.same u ty }

-- a variable has the type its context gives it; a constant the type of its kind (spec 11)
-- (Laws stated on terms that type by construction, not as implications whose premise a random
-- term rarely meets; and `same` and `refines` held apart from the trivial relations, which made
-- every law hold before; review of layers 0-1, B.)
int : Term := Var "Int"
termInt (i : Int) : Term := Lit (IntConst i)

-- a variable has the type its context gives it, a global name the type its declaration gives it
-- (a definition's type, `Define` carrying it, likewise); a constant the type of its kind (spec 11)
TypeOfVar (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (p : Program) (ctx : Context) (x : String) (ty : Term) : Bool :=
  typed a sb t (t.typeOf p (cons (x, ty) ctx) (Var x)) ty
  and typed a sb t (t.typeOf [Declare x ty] [] (Var x)) ty
TypeOfConstant (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (p : Program) (ctx : Context) (i : Int) (u : Float64) (s : String) : Bool :=
  typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (termInt i)) int and typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (Lit (FloatConst u))) (Var "Float64")
  and typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (Lit (StringConst s))) (Var "String")
-- the exponential: a lambda has the dependent function type of its body, applied to an argument
-- of its domain the type of its body with the argument for the variable (3 §2, 3.S5); an
-- application of what is not a function has no type
TypeOfLam (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (p : Program) (ctx : Context) (x : String) (ty : Term) : Bool :=
  typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (Lam x ty (Var x))) (Pi x ty ty)
TypeOfApp (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (p : Program) (ctx : Context) (x : String) (i : Int) : Bool :=
  typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (App (Lam x int (Var x)) (termInt i))) int
  and t.typeOf p ctx (App (termInt i) (termInt i)) == nothing
-- the product, the record and its projection, the sum's injection, a match's arm (3 §2)
TypeOfIntroductions (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (p : Program) (ctx : Context) (i j : Int) (x y : String) : Bool :=
  typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (Pair (termInt i) (termInt j))) (Sigma "_" int int)
  and (x == y or (typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (RecordValue [(x, termInt i), (y, termInt j)])) (Record [(x, int), (y, int)])
                  and typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (Proj (RecordValue [(x, termInt i), (y, termInt j)]) y)) int))
  and typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (Match (termInt i) [(PWild, termInt j)])) int
-- the type formers are types: their role (L2.7) is to form types, of type `U` when their parts are
TypeOfFormers (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (p : Program) (ctx : Context) (x l : String) : Bool :=
  typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (Pi x int int)) Universe and typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (Sigma x int int)) Universe
  and typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (Sum [(l, int)])) Universe and typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (Record [(l, int)])) Universe
  and typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (Subtype x int (Var "true"))) Universe
  and typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (Data x [(l, Var x)])) Universe
-- a local definition is transparent: inside it the name is the value (D-2026-10-13-aa, Q1)
TypeOfLet (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (p : Program) (ctx : Context) (x : String) (i : Int) : Bool :=
  typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (Let x int (termInt i) (Var x))) int
-- `&` joins two laws over one model (5.S6): two Boolean predicates give a Boolean predicate, and
-- when either part is valued in `Law` (laws.lth) the Boolean part is lifted and the conjunction is
-- a `Law` ("a combination of both lifts each Boolean part") [proposed: elaborate.py bite 6,
-- 0984440; stated by luthier-03]
predicateOn (x : String) (c : Term) : Term := Pi x (Var "A") c
conjunctionOf (ctx : Context) (x : String) (l r : Term) : Context :=
  cons ("P", predicateOn x l) (cons ("Q", predicateOn x r) ctx)
amp : Term := App (App (Var "&") (Var "P")) (Var "Q")
TypeOfConjunction (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (p : Program) (ctx : Context) (x : String) : Bool :=
  typed a sb t (t.typeOf p (conjunctionOf ctx x (Var "Bool") (Var "Bool")) amp) (predicateOn x (Var "Bool"))
  and typed a sb t (t.typeOf p (conjunctionOf ctx x (Var "Law") (Var "Bool")) amp) (predicateOn x (Var "Law"))
  and typed a sb t (t.typeOf p (conjunctionOf ctx x (Var "Bool") (Var "Law")) amp) (predicateOn x (Var "Law"))
  and typed a sb t (t.typeOf p (conjunctionOf ctx x (Var "Law") (Var "Law")) amp) (predicateOn x (Var "Law"))
-- the universe is a type, and the world (D-2026-10-13-b); version 0 keeps `U : U` (3.S8)
TypeOfUniverse (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (p : Program) (ctx : Context) : Bool :=
  typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx Universe) Universe and typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx World) Universe

-- `same`, definitional equality of types (3.S20): alpha-equal types are the same, a defined type
-- name is its body, and distinct heads are not the same
SameIsAlpha (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (q : AlphaPair a) : Bool := t.same q.s q.t
SameSeparates (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) : Bool :=
  not (t.same Universe int) and not (t.same int (Var "String")) and not (t.same int (Pi "_" int int))
  -- the names of a record and their order are part of it (3.R1 with D-2026-10-13-x): swapping two
  -- fields, or renaming one, gives another type
  and not (t.same (Record [("a", int), ("b", Var "String")]) (Record [("b", Var "String"), ("a", int)]))
  and not (t.same (Record [("a", int)]) (Record [("c", int)]))

-- refinement: reflexive; a subtype refines its base (3.S6); functions contravariant in the
-- domain and covariant in the codomain (4.R9), over pairs it relates; distinct bases do not refine
-- one another, and a base does not refine a subtype of it
RefinePair (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) : U := { small big : Term | t.refines small big }
RefinesItself (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (ty : Term) : Bool := t.refines ty ty
SubtypeRefinesBase (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (x : String) (ty q : Term) : Bool :=
  t.refines (Subtype x ty q) ty
RefinesFunctions (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (x : String) (d c : RefinePair a sb t) : Bool :=
  t.refines (Pi x d.big c.small) (Pi x d.small c.big)
RefinesSeparates (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (x : String) : Bool :=
  not (t.refines (Var "String") int) and not (t.refines int (Subtype x int (App (App (Var "<") (termInt 0)) (Var x))))

-- 4.R11: inside the branch of a condition `c` in which a variable `x : T` occurs, `x` has the
-- subtype `{ x : T | c }`, and inside the other `{ x : T | not c }`; the same holds of a pattern:
-- in the arm `just y`, the scrutinee is `just y` (stated by the arm's context, as the variable's)
branchesRefine (ctx : Context) (t : Context -> Term -> Bool -> Context) (x : String) (c ty : Term) : Bool :=
  lookup List String Term x (t (cons (x, ty) ctx) c true) == just (Subtype x ty c)
  and lookup List String Term x (t (cons (x, ty) ctx) c false) == just (Subtype x ty (App (Var "not") c))
-- stated on two conditions in which `x` occurs: a predicate applied to it, and `0 < x`
BranchRefines (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (ctx : Context) (x q : String) (ty : Term) : Bool :=
  branchesRefine ctx t.branchContext x (App (Var q) (Var x)) ty
  and branchesRefine ctx t.branchContext x (App (App (Var "<") (termInt 0)) (Var x)) ty

Typing (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) := TypeOfVar a sb & TypeOfConstant a sb & TypeOfLam a sb & TypeOfApp a sb & TypeOfConjunction a sb
  & TypeOfIntroductions a sb & TypeOfFormers a sb & TypeOfLet a sb & TypeOfUniverse a sb & SameIsAlpha a sb
  & SameSeparates a sb & RefinesItself a sb & SubtypeRefinesBase a sb & RefinesFunctions a sb & RefinesSeparates a sb
  & BranchRefines a sb

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- §5 The rules that read types

-- the elaborated acts of a name, and every application in a term with the context it sits in
declaredType (ep : Program) (n : String) : Maybe Term :=
  lookup List String Term n (concat (String * Term) (map (fn (act : Act) { match act { Declare x ty -> [(x, ty)] ; _ -> nil } }) ep))
definedBody (ep : Program) (n : String) : Maybe Term :=
  lookup List String Term n (concat (String * Term) (map (fn (act : Act) { match act { Define x ty b -> [(x, b)] ; _ -> nil } }) ep))
Application = { context : Context, function : Term, argument : Term }
applications (ctx : Context) (u : Term) : List Application := match u {
  App f x -> cons { context := ctx, function := f, argument := x } (((applications ctx f) <> (applications ctx x))) ;
  Lam x ty b -> ((applications ctx ty) <> (applications (cons (x, ty) ctx) b)) ;
  Pi x ty b -> ((applications ctx ty) <> (applications (cons (x, ty) ctx) b)) ;
  Sigma x ty b -> ((applications ctx ty) <> (applications (cons (x, ty) ctx) b)) ;
  Subtype x ty b -> ((applications ctx ty) <> (applications (cons (x, ty) ctx) b)) ;
  Let x ty v b -> ((applications ctx ty) <> (((applications ctx v) <> (applications (cons (x, ty) ctx) b)))) ;
  Pair x y -> ((applications ctx x) <> (applications ctx y)) ;
  Inj l x -> applications ctx x ;
  Match s arms -> ((applications ctx s) <> (armsApplications ctx arms)) ;
  _ -> nil ;
}
armsApplications (ctx : Context) (arms : List (Pattern * Term)) : List Application :=
  concat Application (map (fn (arm : Pattern * Term) { match arm { (q, b) -> applications ctx b } }) arms)
bodyApplications (a : Alpha) (e : Elaboration a) (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : List Application :=
  match definedBody (e.elaborate p) n { nothing -> nil ; just b -> applications nil b }

-- 4.R6: the body of a declared name has its type `T`, or `T -> Bool`, `T -> Failures E`, `Law T`,
-- compared under the theory's own parameters: for `T (a : A) : { ... }` and `T (a : A) := L a`,
-- the parameters are peeled from both before comparing (review of layers 0-1, B); a law may take
-- further quantified parameters after the model, `T -> X -> Bool`
fitsAt (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (ty bt : Term) : Bool :=
  t.same bt ty or endsIn a sb t ty bt
endsIn (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (ty bt : Term) : Bool := match bt {
  Pi x d c -> t.same d ty and verdictType c ; App f arg -> t.same bt (App (Var "Law") ty) ; _ -> false }
verdictType (c : Term) : Bool := match c {
  Var v -> v == "Bool" ; App f arg -> f == Var "Failures" ; Pi x d r -> verdictType r ; _ -> false }
fits (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (ty : Term) (r : Maybe Term) : Bool := match r {
  nothing -> false ;
  just bt -> match ty { Pi x d c -> (match bt { Pi y e f -> t.same d e and fits a sb t c (just f) ; _ -> fitsAt a sb t ty bt }) ;
                        _ -> fitsAt a sb t ty bt } }
violatesR6 (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (e : Elaboration a) (t : Typing a sb) (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  isDeclared p n and isDefined p n and (match declaredType (e.elaborate p) n { nothing -> false ;
    just ty -> match definedBody (e.elaborate p) n { nothing -> false ;
      just b -> not (fits a sb t ty (t.typeOf (e.elaborate p) nil b)) } })

-- 4.R8: `==` only where equality is structural: never on a type that contains an exponential,
-- looked through the program's definitions of type names (fuel: the number of acts, so a
-- recursive `data` is looked through once)
-- (a `data`'s constructors are arrows into it: what is read is their argument types; a name is
-- looked through its definition, or its declaration when it is a theory declared by its record;
-- review of layers 0-1, B)
containsArrow (ep : Program) (fuel : Nat) (ty : Term) : Bool := match ty {
  Pi x d c -> true ;
  Sigma x d c -> containsArrow ep fuel d or containsArrow ep fuel c ;
  Subtype x d q -> containsArrow ep fuel d ;
  Sum kvs -> any List (String * Term) (fn (kv : String * Term) { match kv { (k, v) -> containsArrow ep fuel v } }) kvs ; Data x kvs -> any List (String * Term) (fn (kv : String * Term) { match kv { (k, v) -> any List Term (containsArrow ep fuel) (arguments v) } }) kvs ; Record kvs -> any List (String * Term) (fn (kv : String * Term) { match kv { (k, v) -> containsArrow ep fuel v } }) kvs ;
  App f x -> containsArrow ep fuel f or containsArrow ep fuel x ;
  Var x -> fuel > 0 and (match definedBody ep x {
    just b -> containsArrow ep (fuel - 1) b ;
    nothing -> match declaredType ep x { just (Record kvs) -> any List (String * Term) (fn (kv : String * Term) { match kv { (k, v) -> containsArrow ep (fuel - 1) v } }) kvs ; _ -> false } }) ;
  _ -> false ;
}
arguments (ty : Term) : List Term := match ty { Pi x d c -> cons d (arguments c) ; _ -> nil }
actCount (ep : Program) : Nat := size ep
eqOnArrow (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (ep : Program) (ap : Application) : Bool :=
  match ap.function { App f x -> f == Var "==" and (match t.typeOf ep ap.context x { nothing -> false ;
    just ty -> containsArrow ep (actCount ep) ty }) ; _ -> false }
violatesR8 (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (e : Elaboration a) (t : Typing a sb) (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  any List Application (fn ap { eqOnArrow a sb t (e.elaborate p) ap }) (bodyApplications a e p n)

-- 4.R9: an argument passes where its function's domain is expected only if its base refines the
-- domain's base; a refinement the argument does not carry is an obligation (4.R5, 4.R11), not a
-- failure (review of layers 0-1, B)
-- (a name defined as a subtype is looked through to its base; check.py, bite 2: `WellFormedEbnf`
-- passed where `Ebnf` is expected)
base (ep : Program) (fuel : Nat) (ty : Term) : Term := match ty {
  Subtype x d q -> base ep fuel d ;
  Var x -> if fuel == 0 then ty else (match definedBody ep x { just (Subtype y d q) -> base ep (fuel - 1) d ; _ -> ty }) ;
  _ -> ty }
mismatch (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (ep : Program) (ap : Application) : Bool :=
  match t.typeOf ep ap.context ap.function { nothing -> false ;
    just ft -> match ft { Pi x d c -> (match t.typeOf ep ap.context ap.argument { nothing -> false ;
                                          just at -> not (t.refines (base ep (actCount ep) at) (base ep (actCount ep) d)) }) ;
                          _ -> false } }
violatesR9 (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (e : Elaboration a) (t : Typing a sb) (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  any List Application (fn ap { mismatch a sb t (e.elaborate p) ap }) (bodyApplications a e p n)

-- 6.R1: what `cite name ref checked who` cites is a `Reference` (12.R1): a datum citing the name,
-- whose second argument does not type as `Reference` (check.py, step 4.1)
spine (u : Term) : List Term := match u { App f x -> ((spine f) <> [x]) ; _ -> [u] }
-- kept as a recursion (bite 13b): reads the shape of the application spine (head, first argument, second argument), no iteration
badCitation (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (ep : Program) (n : String) (u : Term) : Bool :=
  match spine u { cons h args -> h == Var "cite" and (match args {
    cons x more -> x == Var n and (match more { cons r rest -> not (typed a sb t (t.typeOf ep nil r) (Var "Reference")) ;
                                                nil -> false }) ;
    nil -> false }) ; nil -> false }
violates6R1 (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (e : Elaboration a) (t : Typing a sb) (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  any List Act (fn (act : Act) { match act { Datum u -> (badCitation a sb t (e.elaborate p) n) u ; _ -> false } }) (e.elaborate p)

-- 4.R11 is a law of the typing (`BranchRefines`): a checker that types branches by it rejects no
-- program the rule accepts. 4.R13 (an operator resolved by the type, one meaning per types) and
-- 4.S23 (implicit arguments from the expected type) are laws of the elaboration (step 2.4).

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- §6 Reports

-- What does not reject is reported (4.S19, 4.S20): a provisional extern (4.R5), a loose function
-- (4.S17: a top-level definition at a bare exponential, until local definitions exist), and a
-- `data` whose constructors no law mentions (4.R3, reported besides). Whether a law characterizes
-- or only compares (4.R10, 4.S20) is the author's judgement, reported by name only.
reportedAs (rs : List Report) (kind n : String) : Bool :=
  any List Report (fn (r : Report) { r.kind == kind and r.name == n }) rs
provisionalExtern (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  any List SurfaceAct (fn act { match act { define x bs t b -> (match b { termBody u -> isExtern u and isProvisionalExtern u ; _ -> false }) ;
                              _ -> false } }) (actsNamed p n)
looseFunction (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  any List SurfaceAct (fn act { match act { define x bs t b -> nonEmptyBinders bs or (match t { just (binop o l r) -> o == "->" ; _ -> false }) ;
                              _ -> false } }) (actsNamed p n)
nonEmptyBinders (bs : List Binder) : Bool := not (isEmpty Binder bs)
ReportsWhen (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (e : Elaboration a) (t : Typing a sb) (kind : String)
            (holds : SurfaceProgram -> String -> Bool) (w : WellFormed a sb e t) (c : Violating holds) : Bool :=
  reportedAs (w.report c.p) kind c.n
ReportsOnlyWhen (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (e : Elaboration a) (t : Typing a sb) (kind : String)
                (holds : SurfaceProgram -> String -> Bool) (w : WellFormed a sb e t) (c : Clean holds) : Bool :=
  not (reportedAs (w.report c.p) kind c.n)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- §7 WellFormed

-- A checker reports every failure of each rule, and no failure where a complete predicate finds
-- none (4.R1, 4.R4, 4.R5, 4.R7); the predicates still partial have the first law only. It reports
-- only about the program's names, and reports what does not reject, an unclaimed law (4.S14)
-- among it.
WellFormed (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (e : Elaboration a) (t : Typing a sb) :=
  ReportsViolations a sb e t "4.R1" violatesR1 & ReportsNoFalseFailure a sb e t "4.R1" violatesR1
  & ReportsViolations a sb e t "4.R2" violatesR2Exists & ReportsViolations a sb e t "4.R3" violatesR3
  & ReportsViolations a sb e t "4.R4" violatesR4 & ReportsNoFalseFailure a sb e t "4.R4" violatesR4
  & ReportsViolations a sb e t "4.R5" violatesR5 & ReportsNoFalseFailure a sb e t "4.R5" violatesR5
  & ReportsViolations a sb e t "4.R6" (violatesR6 a sb e t)
  & ReportsViolations a sb e t "4.R7" violatesR7 & ReportsNoFalseFailure a sb e t "4.R7" violatesR7
  & ReportsViolations a sb e t "4.R8" (violatesR8 a sb e t) & ReportsViolations a sb e t "4.R9" (violatesR9 a sb e t)
  & ReportsViolations a sb e t "4.R12" violatesR12 & ReportsViolations a sb e t "2.R1" violatesR2R1
  & ReportsViolations a sb e t "2.R6" violatesR2R6 & ReportsViolations a sb e t "4.R13" violatesR13
  & ReportsViolations a sb e t "6.R1" (violates6R1 a sb e t) & ReportsOnItsNames a sb e t
  & ReportsWhen a sb e t "unclaimed" violatesS14 & ReportsOnlyWhen a sb e t "unclaimed" violatesS14
  & ReportsWhen a sb e t "provisional" provisionalExtern & ReportsOnlyWhen a sb e t "provisional" provisionalExtern
  & ReportsWhen a sb e t "loose" looseFunction & ReportsOnlyWhen a sb e t "loose" looseFunction
